/-!
# The short-root type-G2 carrier over the prime field of characteristic three

The short-root type-`G₂` carrier over `ℤ` is the Kostant toral closure of the seven-dimensional
module `V(ϖ₁)` inside `GL₇`: the largest Hopf ideal of `O(GL₇/ℤ)` killed by the coordinate maps of
the four numbered simple root subgroups and of the rank-two weight torus. This file forms the
companion carrier over the prime field `𝔽₃`: the closed subgroup scheme of `GL₇` over `𝔽₃`
generated by the reductions of those same coordinate maps.

Over `𝔽₃` the defining ideal is again the largest Hopf ideal killed by the generators, this time by
construction. That maximality is what lets a homomorphism to `GL₇` satisfying the generator
equations be restricted to an endomorphism of the carrier, and it is what the special isogeny of
type `G₂` in characteristic three needs. It is not available for the base change of the integral
carrier, whose defining ideal is maximal over `ℤ` only: new equations can appear over a base that
is not flat. The two carriers are therefore compared in one direction only, and no flatness is
asserted.

The root subgroups and the weight torus are the reductions of the integral ones, so their matrices
and the pinning equation between them are not re-derived.

The carrier is not identified with the pinned simply connected group scheme of type `G₂`, and
constructions on it transfer to that group scheme only along such an identification, once one is
proved.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.generator`: the reduced coordinate maps of the four numbered
  simple root subgroups and of the weight torus.
* `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.definingIdeal`: the largest Hopf ideal of `O(GL₇/𝔽₃)` they kill.
* `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.groupScheme`: the closed subgroup scheme of `GL₇` over `𝔽₃` they
  generate, with `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.carrierι` its closed immersion into `GL₇`.
* `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.rootSubgroup` and
  `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.weightTorus`: those generators, factored through it.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.groupScheme_hom_ext`: a morphism out of the carrier is
  determined by its restrictions to the four numbered root subgroups and to the weight torus.
* `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.baseChangePresentationIdeal_le_definingIdeal`: the carrier is a
  closed subgroup scheme of the base change of the integral short-root carrier.

## References

The construction is the Chevalley--Demazure construction on the seven-dimensional module, carried
out over the prime field; see J. E. Humphreys, *Linear Algebraic Groups*, §26, and R. W. Carter,
*Simple Groups of Lie Type*, §§4.4 and 7.1. The weight conventions follow N. Bourbaki, *Lie Groups
and Lie Algebras, Chapters 4--6*, Plate IX. The reason the prime field, rather than `ℤ`, is the
base for a carrier carrying the special isogeny is the maximality of the defining ideal explained
above; see R. Steinberg, *Endomorphisms of linear algebraic groups*, Memoirs AMS **80** (1968),
§11.
-/

public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory

namespace TauCeti.G2ShortRoot

open TauCeti.DynkinType
open TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra

attribute [local instance 100] LieRing.ofAssociativeRing
attribute [local instance high] Algebra.toModule

local notation "CM" => CartanMatrix.G₂
local notation "rootGen" => TauCeti.serreRootGenerator CM
local notation "cartanGen" => TauCeti.serreH ℚ CM

namespace PrimeField

/-- The coordinate Hopf algebra receiving a reduced root-subgroup or weight-torus generator: that
of the additive group over `𝔽₃` at a root index, and that of the rank-two split torus over `𝔽₃` at
the torus index. -/
noncomputable abbrev generatorCodomain :
    (Fin 2 ⊕ Fin 2) ⊕ Unit → CommHopfAlgCat (ZMod 3)
  | .inl _ => AdditiveGroup.coordinateHopfAlgebra (ZMod 3)
  | .inr _ => (DiagonalizableGroup.coordinateRing (ZMod 3)
      (SplitTorus.characterGroup (Fin 2))).obj

/-- The generating coordinate maps of the short-root type-`G₂` carrier over `𝔽₃`: the reductions of
the four numbered simple root-subgroup coordinate maps and of the weight-torus coordinate map,
transported into the coordinate Hopf algebras formed directly over `𝔽₃`. -/
noncomputable def generator :
    ∀ j, TauCeti.GeneralLinear.coordinateHopfAlgebra (ZMod 3) 7 ⟶ generatorCodomain j
  | .inl k => kostantRootSubgroupBaseChangePresentationCoordinateMap rootGen cartanGen rep
      lattice.toAddSubgroup rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice
      isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator latticeBasis (ZMod 3) k
  | .inr _ => TauCeti.GeneralLinear.weightTorusBaseChangeCoordinateMap ℤ (ZMod 3) weight

/-- At a root index the generating family is the reduced root-subgroup coordinate map. -/
theorem generator_inl (k : Fin 2 ⊕ Fin 2) :
    generator (.inl k) =
      kostantRootSubgroupBaseChangePresentationCoordinateMap rootGen cartanGen rep
        lattice.toAddSubgroup rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice
        isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator latticeBasis (ZMod 3) k := by
  rw [generator]

/-- At the torus index the generating family is the reduced weight-torus coordinate map. -/
theorem generator_inr :
    generator (.inr ()) =
      TauCeti.GeneralLinear.weightTorusBaseChangeCoordinateMap ℤ (ZMod 3) weight := by
  rw [generator]

/-- The Hopf ideal cutting out the short-root type-`G₂` carrier over `𝔽₃` inside `GL₇`: the largest
Hopf ideal of `O(GL₇/𝔽₃)` killed by all the reduced generators. -/
noncomputable def definingIdeal :
    HopfIdeal (ZMod 3) (TauCeti.GeneralLinear.coordinateHopfAlgebra (ZMod 3) 7) :=
  CommHopfAlgCat.commonKernelHopfIdeal generator

/-- The defining ideal is the common-kernel ideal of the reduced generators. -/
theorem definingIdeal_def :
    definingIdeal = CommHopfAlgCat.commonKernelHopfIdeal generator := by
  rw [definingIdeal]

/-- **The short-root type-`G₂` carrier over `𝔽₃`**: the closed subgroup scheme of `GL₇` over `𝔽₃`
generated by the reductions of the numbered simple root subgroups and of the weight torus. -/
noncomputable abbrev groupScheme : Grp (Over (Spec (CommRingCat.of (ZMod 3)))) :=
  TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatedGroupScheme 7 generator

/-- The quotient-spectrum presentation of the carrier over `𝔽₃`. -/
theorem groupScheme_def :
    groupScheme = CommHopfAlgCat.quotientSpec
      (TauCeti.GeneralLinear.coordinateHopfAlgebra (ZMod 3) 7) definingIdeal := by
  rw [definingIdeal_def]
  exact TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatedGroupScheme_def 7 generator

/-- The canonical inclusion of the carrier over `𝔽₃` into `GL₇`. -/
noncomputable def carrierι : groupScheme ⟶ TauCeti.GeneralLinear.groupScheme (ZMod 3) 7 :=
  TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatedGroupSchemeι 7 generator

/-- The ambient inclusion is the one of the generated subgroup scheme. -/
theorem carrierι_def :
    carrierι = TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatedGroupSchemeι 7 generator := by
  rw [carrierι]

/-- The carrier over `𝔽₃` is a closed subgroup scheme of `GL₇`. -/
instance isClosedImmersion_carrierι : IsClosedImmersion carrierι.hom.hom.left := by
  rw [carrierι]
  exact TauCeti.GeneralLinear.isClosedImmersion_generatedGroupSchemeι 7 generator

/-- A positive or negative numbered simple root subgroup of the carrier over `𝔽₃`. -/
noncomputable def rootSubgroup (k : Fin 2 ⊕ Fin 2) :
    AdditiveGroup.groupScheme (ZMod 3) ⟶ groupScheme :=
  eqToHom (AdditiveGroup.groupScheme_def (ZMod 3)) ≫
    TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatorToGeneratedGroupScheme 7 generator (.inl k)

/-- The numbered root subgroup is the generator of the generated subgroup scheme it indexes. -/
theorem rootSubgroup_def (k : Fin 2 ⊕ Fin 2) :
    rootSubgroup k =
      eqToHom (AdditiveGroup.groupScheme_def (ZMod 3)) ≫
        TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatorToGeneratedGroupScheme 7 generator (.inl k) := by
  rw [rootSubgroup]

/-- The rank-two split weight torus in the carrier over `𝔽₃`. -/
noncomputable def weightTorus : SplitTorus.groupScheme (ZMod 3) (Fin 2) ⟶ groupScheme :=
  eqToHom (DiagonalizableGroup.groupScheme_def (ZMod 3) (SplitTorus.characterGroup (Fin 2))) ≫
    TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatorToGeneratedGroupScheme 7 generator (.inr ())

/-- The weight torus is the generator of the generated subgroup scheme it indexes. -/
theorem weightTorus_def :
    weightTorus =
      eqToHom
        (DiagonalizableGroup.groupScheme_def (ZMod 3) (SplitTorus.characterGroup (Fin 2))) ≫
        TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatorToGeneratedGroupScheme 7 generator (.inr ()) := by
  rw [weightTorus]

/-- Including a numbered root subgroup into `GL₇` recovers the reduced generating morphism. -/
@[simp]
theorem rootSubgroup_comp_carrierι (k : Fin 2 ⊕ Fin 2) :
    rootSubgroup k ≫ carrierι =
      eqToHom (AdditiveGroup.groupScheme_def (ZMod 3)) ≫
        (hopfSpec (CommRingCat.of (ZMod 3))).map (generator (.inl k)).op ≫
          eqToHom (TauCeti.GeneralLinear.groupScheme_def (ZMod 3) 7).symm := by
  rw [rootSubgroup_def, carrierι_def, Category.assoc,
    TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatorToGeneratedGroupScheme_comp_ι]

/-- Including the weight torus into `GL₇` recovers the reduced generating morphism. -/
@[simp]
theorem weightTorus_comp_carrierι :
    weightTorus ≫ carrierι =
      eqToHom
          (DiagonalizableGroup.groupScheme_def (ZMod 3) (SplitTorus.characterGroup (Fin 2))) ≫
        (hopfSpec (CommRingCat.of (ZMod 3))).map (generator (.inr ())).op ≫
          eqToHom (TauCeti.GeneralLinear.groupScheme_def (ZMod 3) 7).symm := by
  rw [weightTorus_def, carrierι_def, Category.assoc,
    TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatorToGeneratedGroupScheme_comp_ι]

/-- Two morphisms out of the carrier over `𝔽₃` agree when they agree on all four numbered simple
root subgroups and on the weight torus. -/
@[ext]
theorem groupScheme_hom_ext {Y : _root_.CommHopfAlgCat.{0} (ZMod 3)}
    (f g : groupScheme ⟶ (hopfSpec (CommRingCat.of (ZMod 3))).obj (Opposite.op Y))
    (hroot : ∀ k, rootSubgroup k ≫ f = rootSubgroup k ≫ g)
    (htorus : weightTorus ≫ f = weightTorus ≫ g) : f = g := by
  apply (cancel_epi (eqToHom groupScheme_def.symm)).1
  refine CommHopfAlgCat.hom_ext_of_preimage_unop_eq
    (eqToHom groupScheme_def.symm ≫ f) (eqToHom groupScheme_def.symm ≫ g) ?_
  apply CommHopfAlgCat.commonKernelLift_hom_ext generator
  rintro (k | u)
  · refine CommHopfAlgCat.preimage_unop_comp_eq_of_hopfSpec_map_comp_eq _
      (eqToHom groupScheme_def.symm ≫ f) (eqToHom groupScheme_def.symm ≫ g) ?_
    have hk := hroot k
    rw [rootSubgroup_def, TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatorToGeneratedGroupScheme_def,
      Category.assoc, Category.assoc] at hk
    exact (cancel_epi (eqToHom (AdditiveGroup.groupScheme_def (ZMod 3)))).1 hk
  · rcases u with ⟨⟩
    refine CommHopfAlgCat.preimage_unop_comp_eq_of_hopfSpec_map_comp_eq _
      (eqToHom groupScheme_def.symm ≫ f) (eqToHom groupScheme_def.symm ≫ g) ?_
    rw [weightTorus_def, TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatorToGeneratedGroupScheme_def,
      Category.assoc, Category.assoc] at htorus
    exact (cancel_epi (eqToHom
      (DiagonalizableGroup.groupScheme_def (ZMod 3)
        (SplitTorus.characterGroup (Fin 2))))).1 htorus

/-- **The carrier over `𝔽₃` is a closed subgroup scheme of the base change of the integral
short-root carrier.** The reverse containment is not claimed: the integral defining ideal is the
largest Hopf ideal killed by the generators over `ℤ` only, and new equations can appear over a base
that is not flat. -/
theorem baseChangePresentationIdeal_le_definingIdeal :
    kostantToralBaseChangePresentationIdeal rootGen cartanGen rep lattice.toAddSubgroup
        rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator latticeBasis weight
        (ZMod 3) ≤
      definingIdeal := by
  have h := kostantToralBaseChangePresentationIdeal_le_commonKernelHopfIdeal rootGen cartanGen rep
    lattice.toAddSubgroup rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator
    latticeBasis weight (ZMod 3)
  dsimp only at h
  rw [CommHopfAlgCat.le_commonKernelHopfIdeal_iff] at h
  rw [definingIdeal_def, CommHopfAlgCat.le_commonKernelHopfIdeal_iff]
  rintro (k | u)
  · simpa only [generator_inl] using h (.inl k)
  · rcases u with ⟨⟩
    rw [generator_inr]
    exact h (.inr ())

end PrimeField

end TauCeti.G2ShortRoot
